item.description:
Members:<a class="internal-link" data-href="API/Interfaces/Animation.md" href="api/interfaces/animation.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Animation</a> - Methods for creating and handling animation<br>
<a class="internal-link" data-href="API/Interfaces/Layout.md" href="api/interfaces/layout.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Layout</a> - Handles layouts and provides template layoutsMethods:GetUI_3D -&gt; UIContainerfunction Cinnamon.GetUI_3D(ScreenGui) : UIContainer Clears out and destroys child objects without destroying the container
NewContainer -&gt; UIContainerfunction Cinnamon.NewContainer( ScreenGui, Origin : CFrame
) : UIContainer Creates a new UI container
NewScreenContainer -&gt; ScreenContainerfunction Cinnamon.NewScreenContainer( ScreenGui, DisplayDistance : number
) : ScreenContainer Creates a new ScreenContainer
Destroy -&gt; nilfunction Cinnamon.Destroy( UI3D_Object : {Destroy : (T) -&gt; nil},
) : nil Deletes anything with a internal destroy method

Handles layouts and provides template layoutsMethods:ApplyLayout -&gt; nilfunction ApplyLayout( Elements : {Element}, Layout : {CFrame}
) : nil Applies the layout to a table of elements
Templates:
Radial - Places elements in a ring formationfunction Radial(Elements : {Lookup.Element}, Props : { Origin : CFrame, Distance: number, StartAngle : number, Padding : number, Axis : Vector3 }
)
List - Places elements in straight linefunction List(Elements : {Lookup.Element}, Props : { Origin : CFrame, FillDirection : Vector3, UpDirection : Vector3, ItemsUntilWrap : number, Padding : number, }
)
Grid - Places elements on a gridfunction Grid(Elements : {Lookup.Element}, Props : { Origin : CFrame, LookDirection : Vector3, RowSize : number, ColumnSize : number, Padding : Vector2 }
)
Quad bezier - Places Elements along a bezier curvefunction QuadBezier(Elements : {Lookup.Element}, Props : { Origin : CFrame, P1 : CFrame, Goal : CFrame, Padding : number }
)
PlaceFromUDim2 - Places Elements according to its UI position, relative to its container originfunction PlaceFromUDim2( Elements : {Lookup.Element}, DisplayDistance
)

Methods for creating and managing <a class="internal-link" data-href="API/Objects/Animatables.md" href="api/objects/animatables.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">animations</a>.Methods:
Tween -&gt; Tweenfunction Animation.Tween&lt;T&gt;( _Instance : Instance, Property : string, Goal : T, EasingDirection : string, EasingStyle : string, Speed : number
) : Tween&lt;T&gt; Creates tween animation
Spring -&gt; Spring function Spring&lt;T&gt;( _Instance : Instance, Property : string, Goal : T, Frequency : number, Damping : number, Response : number, Speed : number ) : Spring&lt;T&gt; Creates spring animation
Bezier -&gt; Bezierfunction Bezier&lt;T&gt;( _Instance : Instance, Property : string, Goal : T, EasingDirection : string, EasingStyle : string, P1 : T, P2 : T, Speed : number
) : Bezier&lt;T&gt; Creates bezier animation
Oscillator -&gt; Oscillatorfunction Oscillator&lt;T&gt;( _Instance : Instance, Property : string, Goal : T, Frequency : number, Phase : number, EasingDirection : string, EasingStyle : string, WaveForm : WaveForm, Speed : number
) : Oscillator&lt;T&gt; Creates oscillation animation
BatchAnimation -&gt; BatchAnimationfunction BatchAnimation&lt;T&gt;( AnimationType : "Tween" | "Spring" | "Bezier" | "Oscillator", _Instances : {Instance | Element}, Props : {Property : string}, GroupData : {Goal : {T},P1 : {T},P2 : {T},Phase : {number}}
) : BatchAnimation Creates batch animation
SetGoal -&gt; nilfunction SetGoal&lt;T&gt;(Animated : Animatable&lt;T&gt;,Goal : T) -&gt; nil Sets the goal of a single animation
Reset -&gt; nilfunction Reset&lt;T&gt;(Animated : Animatable&lt;T&gt;) -&gt; nil Resets an animation

Holds <a class="internal-link" data-href="API/Objects/Element.md" href="api/objects/element.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Elements</a> and positions them on the screen.Properties:Enabled : Boolean
Enables/Disables child objects
Debug : Boolean
Adds/Removes itself and its child objects from the debug visualiser
DisplayDistance : number
How far the elements are from the screen
Members: Elements : {Element}
The Elements being stored
UI : ScreenGui
The UI that stores your Elements
Methods:Element -&gt; Elementfunction Container:Element(Props : { UI : GuiObject, Offset : CFrame, Resolution : Vector2, Face : Enum.NormalId }
) : Element creates a new element
Clear -&gt; nilfunction Container:Clear() : nil Clears out and destroys child objects without destroying the container
UDim2ToCFrame -&gt; CFramefunction Container:UDim2ToCFrame( Position : UDim2, ViewPortSize : Vector2, DisplayDistance : number
) : CFrame Projects UDim2 to a position relative to the origin
Partsize -&gt; Vector3
function Container:UDim2ToCFrame( Position : UDim2, ViewPortSize : Vector2,
) : CFrame Calculate how large a element should be using position and viewport size

Animatable (Base class, not usable)type Animatable&lt;T&gt; = { Goal : T, Type : "Tween" | "Spring" | "Bezier" | "Oscillator", Instance : Instance, Property : string, Enabled : boolean, Speed : number, Destroy : (Animatable&lt;T&gt;), Time : number, Origin : T, }
Tweens:type Tween&lt;T&gt; = Animatable&lt;T&gt; &amp; { EasingDirection : string, EasingStyle : string, Time : number, Origin : T, Type : "Tween"
}
Springs:type Spring&lt;T&gt; = Animatable&lt;T&gt; &amp; { k1 : number, k2 : number, k3 : number, Previous : T, Velocity : T, Type : "Spring"
}
Beziers:type Bezier&lt;T&gt; = Tween&lt;T&gt; &amp; { P1 : T, P2 : T, Type : "Bezier"
}
Oscillators:type Oscillator&lt;T&gt; = Tween&lt;T&gt; &amp; { Type : "Oscillator", Frequency : number, Phase : number, WaveForm : (Time : number,Frequency : number,Phase : number) -&gt; number
}
Batch Animation:type BatchAnimation&lt;T&gt; = {Animatable&lt;T&gt;} &amp; { SetEnabled : (BatchAnimation&lt;T&gt;,Enabled : Boolean) -&gt; nil, SetGoals : (BatchAnimation&lt;T&gt;,Goal : {T}) -&gt; nil,
}
